-- check/bad: §11's module-rule namespace clash, in the small. A module's
-- `pub` values are ONE namespace, so `eq` here is `Version`'s method and
-- `Colour`'s at the same time — and `==` on a `Colour` finds it and fails
-- to unify. Roc hit this and moved to a per-type block in October 2025;
-- `plans/static-dispatch-spike.md` §0 and §11 record that we may need to
-- as well, and M8 counts how often it would bite.
--
-- Because every lookup is keyed on `(TypeId, name)` (§1.2), a block form
-- would be a front-end change and nothing else — which is why this is a
-- fixture and not a bug.
pub type Version
    = Version Int


pub type Colour
    = Red
    | Green


pub eq : Version, Version -> Bool
eq a b =
    True


pub sameColour : Colour, Colour -> Bool
sameColour a b =
    a == b
